<title>UK: UK Treasury values stable stg rate, has no target.</title>
<headline>UK Treasury values stable stg rate, has no target.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury reaffirmed on Thursday that it has no target for sterling.</p>
<p>&quot;The government recognises the value of a stable exchange rate but does not have a target for sterling. The exchange rate is only one of many factors that has to be taken into account of in policy decisions,&quot; Economic Secretary Angela Knight said in a written parliamentary answer.</p>
<p>&quot;Monetary policy is, and will continue to be, aimed at achieving the government's inflation target of 2-1/2 percent or less,&quot; she added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7767</p>
